      "locale": "en",
      "voice": "Charon",
      "spokenText": "Try an invented training example, not an actual laboratory result. Residue R in peppers is zero point one two milligrams per kilogram of food, and the portion weighs two hundred and fifty grams. Assume a homogeneous portion and matching analysed-part and mass bases. First convert grams to kilograms: two hundred and fifty grams is zero point two five zero kilograms. Multiply concentration by food mass. Kilograms of food cancel, leaving zero point zero three zero milligrams of residue. As a cross-check, that equals thirty micrograms. We have calculated residue mass in this portion only. We have not calculated absorption, the rest of the diet or water intake, or shipment compliance.",
